  "title": "Frankl's union-closed sets conjecture",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture Let $F$ be a finite family of finite sets, not all empty, that is closed under taking unions. Then there exists $x$ such that $x$ is an element of at least half the members of $F$.",
